@nsobid-4B159F0F7A360669738390EE8657B4F0

# ASTRAL CHAIN 1.0.1 - Double Buffering

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces a two-texture swapchain.
//
// The display setup creates three window textures and passes all of them to
// nvnWindowBuilderSetTextures. Passing a count of 2 makes the window cycle
// through the first two only, so the CPU can run at most one frame ahead of
// scanout, cutting a frame of input latency. The final render target is
// picked as window textures + acquired index * 0xC0, so the third texture
// is simply never used.

@enabled
009E8D68 41008052   // MOV W1,#2 for nvnWindowBuilderSetTextures (was MOV W1,#3)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against ASTRAL CHAIN 1.0.1 (PlatinumGames "Hw"
// framework, PRJ_036, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was
// located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
